{title: The Greatest of These}
{subtitle: 1 Corinthians 13}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebm/Gb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I could sing like the [Dm7]angels
[Gm]I could speak in every [Eb]tongue
[Bb]But without love I'm [Dm7]a clanging gong
[Eb]A song that's never [Ebm]sung
[Bb]I could move ev[Dm7]ery mountain
[Gm]Give away all that [Ebm]I own
[Bb]But without love I gain [Dm7]nothing
[Eb]I'm standing here a[Ebm]lone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Love is patient, [Dm7]love is kind
[Eb]Keeps no record of [Ebm]wrongs
It bears all [Bb]things, believes all [Dm7]things
Hopes [Eb]all things, endures [Ebm]all things
Love never [Bb]ends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When I was a [Dm7]child I spoke like a [Gm]child
Thought the way that children [Ebm]do
[Bb]Now we see a dim reflec[Dm7]tion in a mirror
[Eb]But then face to face [Ebm]with you
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Faith and hope [Dm7]and love remain
These [Eb]three, these [Bb]three
But the [Cm7]greatest of these
The [F]greatest of these is [Bb]love [Dm7][Eb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ebm]Love never [Bb]ends [Dm7][Eb]
[Ebm]Love never [Bb]ends
{end_of_verse}

